The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=-7$) is the interval between $x=-8$ and $x=-4$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
g'(-7)&\approx\dfrac{g(-4)-g(-8)}{-4-(-8)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{77-85}{4}
\\\\
&=-2
\end{align}$
